  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression? \\[\\frac{2+4+6}{1+3+5} - \\frac{1+3+5}{2+4+6}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( -1 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\dfrac{5}{36} \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\dfrac{7}{12} \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\dfrac{49}{20} \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\dfrac{43}{3} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First evaluate the sums: \\(2+4+6=12\\) and \\(1+3+5=9\\). Reducing the fractions and then using a common denominator gives\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{9}{12}\n=\\frac43-\\frac34\n=\\frac{16}{12}-\\frac9{12}\n=\\boxed{\\frac7{12}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{C}\\).",
